{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall gird them with a sash.</b> The sash includes [that of] Aaron and his sons, and likewise the breeches. After mentioning them, he proceeds to explicate Aaron and his sons, like \"and she opened and saw him, the child\" (above, Exodus 2:6)." "<b>And the word וחבשת.</b> Like \"I shall not be a חובש\" (Isaiah 3:7)." "<b>And you shall fill.</b> The opinion of the Aramaic translator [is] like ומלאו יָדָיו (Ezekiel 43:26). But what is done with the phrase מלוא ידכם היום (below, Exodus 29:22)? The Gaon [Saadia] explained: יד = obligation. And others said that מלואים is because they are complete, full, and accustomed. Now what will they do with the phrase ומלאו יָדָיו (Ezekiel 43:26)?"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {2 "The lemma reads ומלאת; Ibn Ezra then discusses the translator's rendering as if it were a different form. Retained both forms as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:03.327533165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}